CHECK:LINE_SPACING: Please don't use multiple blank lines
#119: FILE: drivers/iommu/amd_iommu.c:1838:
 
+

Vertical space is wasted given the limited number of lines an
editor window can display when multiple blank lines are used.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#spaces

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!domain->gcr3_tbl"
#253: FILE: drivers/iommu/amd_iommu.c:3132:
+	if (domain->gcr3_tbl == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#305: FILE: drivers/iommu/amd_iommu_proto.h:42:
+extern int amd_iommu_domain_enable_v2(struct iommu_domain *dom, int pasids);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#352: FILE: drivers/iommu/amd_iommu_types.h:308:
+#define PD_IOMMUV2_MASK		(1UL << 3) /* domain has gcr3 table */

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

